actor.\n\nThus, the $\\text{GCF}$ of $9m,$ $15n,$ and $21n$ is $3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459247 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054687 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "92176bb0-84dc-5fa4-8154-e974c05fff06" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Greatest Common Factor of a Number and a Variable Expression"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33d48035-29a7-56fd-b211-408d2e26086e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458728} {:answer/id #uuid "861d6513-9da3-5b79-90cb-df2c8fb7fb07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458862} {:answer/id #uuid "be98c2cb-b8ce-5072-9fe7-4ba4e1e6bebb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458969} {:answer/id #uuid "d8dfedc0-a7d0-5e7d-94aa-4d3b670304a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459008} {:answer/id #uuid "dac4904b-ca7c-59dc-9146-97841daa82ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459012}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "33d48035-29a7-56fd-b211-408d2e26086e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458728} :answer-field/id #uuid "fc741d96-18c5-57f9-80a0-24952d4e2dd9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459200}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6e1d2ce7-d4cf-5db3-8147-0127083518c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-359085" :question/problem "What is the greatest common factor of $12$ and $18z?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the GCF, we list the factors of the coefficients and identify any common variable factors in the expressions.\n\nThe factors of $12$ are\n\n$$\n1,\\,2,\\,3,\\,4,\\,6,\\,12.\n$$\n\nThe factors of $18$ are\n\n$$\n1,\\,2,\\,3,\\,6,\\,9,\\,18.\n$$\n\nThe common factors of $12$ and $18$ are\n\n$$\n1,\\,2,\\,3,\\,6.\n$$\n\nThe greatest of these common factors is $6.$\n\nNow we look at the variable factors. Since $12$ has no variable and $18z$ contains $z,$ there are no variable factors in common.\n\nThus, the greatest common factor of $12$ and $18z$ is $6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186459281 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054756 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ee5e58b3-f6d7-56e2-bccd-97095e94495e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Greatest Common Factor of Three Variable Expressions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d0587a5-0b6e-5f1b-80bf-674ce77be511" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458716} {:answer/id #uuid "2e6064de-66ea-5fbd-ab8d-7e4c4e6b630e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458718} {:answer/id #uuid "82ab65fa-3b31-50e4-9e89-dbe23a5e77d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458859} {:answer/id #uuid "d28bc8d6-95bf-52b9-86e4-b4b24550d8c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458994} {:answer/id #uuid "eefa4bbc-677a-51b7-80f7-7b17f7545b58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459051}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e6064de-66ea-5fbd-ab8d-7e4c4e6b630e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6z" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186458718} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba6ed45d-4a3c-5326-b189-87d89d8df9ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186459166}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c0cc76fa-54f2-57a0-bbfe-46b112544e48" :question/math-academy-id "q-359107" :question/problem "Find the $\\text{GCF}$ of $12z$, $18z,$ and $30z.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the GCF, we list the factors of the coefficients and identify any common variable factors in the expressions.\n\nThe factors of $12$ are\n\n$$\n1,\\,2,\\,3,\\,4,\\,6,\\,12.\n$$\n\nThe factors of $18$ are\n\n$$\n1,\\,2,\\,3,\\,6,\\,9,\\,18.\n$$\n\nThe factors of $30$ are\n\n$$\n1,\\,2,\\,3,\\,5,\\,6,\\,10,\\,15,\\,30.\n$$\n\nThe common factors of $12,$ $18,$ and $30$ are\n\n$$\n1,\\,2,\\,3,\\,6.\n$$\n\nThe greatest of these common factors is $6.$\n\nNow we look at the variable factors. The expressions $12z,$ $18z,$ and $30z$ all contain $z.$\n\nThus, the $\\text{GCF}$ of $12z,$ $18z,$ and $30z$ is $6z.$"}]}
